JavBrain
I want to... [
	Search [
		Press **Space**
		**Type** to filter across all file contents and filenames. Results auto-expand with highlighted snippets.
		Press **Escape** to close and return to the full list.
		**Tab** to cycle search modes: fuzzy, all, any, exact.
		**Ctrl+left** and **ctrl+right** to expand and collapse all groups.
		**Arrows** to traverse and expand/collapse groups
	]
	Navigate results [
		**Up/Down** moves through files and match lines.
		**Left** collapses a group or jumps to parent.
		**Right** expands a group.
		**Ctrl+Left** collapses all.
		**Ctrl+Right** expands all. Enter opens the selected file or match line.
	]
	Browse a file [
		Click or press Enter on any file to open it.
		.jav files render with nested colored sections and a table of contents sidebar.
		.txt files render as plain text.
		Code files with ==== delimiters render flat with section headers. These are used to show multiple code files within one entry.
	]
	Use the table of contents [
		Press **Space** to focus the Table of Contents sidebar.
		**Up/Down** to traverse sections.
		**Left/Right** to collapse/expand.
		**Ctrl+Left/Right** to collapse/expand all.
		**Enter** to copy the selected section.
		**Right-click** a section to copy it.
		**Space** or **Escape** to unfocus.
	]
	Switch themes [
		Press **T** to toggle between light and dark.
	]
]
How to write .jav files [
	What is .jav? [
		Simple bracket based language for novel writing in vs code/codium. Allows simple outlining that is more visually informative than markdown, giving "blocks" that author can nest freely.
	]
	Create a named section [
		\\Sections nest freely.\\
		\\content can be in section or in subsections, like CHAPTER ➢ SCENE ➢ BEAT.\\
		\\Generally I put notes for the section above it, like here \\
		Title [
			\\notes for the section\\
			Scene [
				Beat [
					It was a dark and stormy night...
				]
			]
		]
	]
	Other text markup [
		*text* for italic.
		**text** for bold.
		\text\ for inline notes.
		\\text\\ for callout blocks.
		Straight quotes render as curly.
		Each line is a paragraph.
		Lines starting with - · ● ▶ • or numbers skip paragraph indent.
	]
]